"title": "1. Getting started",
"html": "<p>The Opsis QA client portal shows how every customer call your CSRs handle was scored, why it booked or didn't, and what to coach next. It only ever shows your own company's calls — never other clients, Opsis staffing or billing.</p>\n<h3>Signing in</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>garageco.opsiscx.com</strong>.</li>\n<li>First time: open the invite email from your account admin and click the sign-in link. The link works for 24 hours.</li>\n<li>Set your own password when asked. After that, sign in with your email and password.</li>\n<li>Forgot your password? Ask your account admin to click <strong>Resend</strong> next to your name on Team &amp; access.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Your name, role and brand show at the bottom of the left menu, with <strong>Sign out</strong> below them. Some accounts also see a <strong>Classic view</strong> link that switches back to the older portal.</p>\n<h3>What your role lets you do</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Role</th>\n<th>Sees</th>\n<th>Can change</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Account admin</td>\n<td>All brands, every page, Your Setup</td>\n<td>Scores (instantly), knowledge base, QA settings, people, portal branding</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brand manager</td>\n<td>One brand or all brands</td>\n<td>Adds notes, sends score change requests to the admin</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RM (regional manager)</td>\n<td>Their whole brand</td>\n<td>Notes, score change requests, coaching for their CSRs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GM (general manager)</td>\n<td>Their location only</td>\n<td>Notes, score change requests, coaching for their CSRs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Viewer</td>\n<td>One brand or all brands</td>\n<td>Nothing — read-only, can play calls and ask the AI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CSR</td>\n<td>Their own Coaching Hub only</td>\n<td>Nothing — can ask their coach questions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A login locked to one brand never sees another brand's calls or recordings. If a page in this manual is missing from your menu, your role doesn't include it.</p>",
