"id": "3-performance-pages",
"title": "3. Performance pages",
"html": "<p>These pages answer \"how are we doing and why\" for the dates and brands at the top.</p>\n<h3>Overview</h3>\n<p>Your home page. Start here every morning.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Headline numbers</strong> across the top: customer conversations, average QA score, booking rate, booking ask rate, card ask rate and average order value. Each shows its change versus the previous period.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance by Brand</strong> — click a brand to see why it's trending the way it is.</li>\n<li><strong>Top Coaching Opportunities</strong> — the busiest CSRs who ask for the booking least often.</li>\n<li><strong>Call Flow Performance</strong> — how often each step of the call flow is done when it applies. Click a step to hear calls that missed it.</li>\n<li><strong>Needs Attention</strong> — upset customers, low scores and controllable misses: the same lists as the 8am daily summary.</li>\n<li><strong>Calls to Review</strong> — winnable calls that didn't book and scored 40 or lower.</li>\n<li><strong>First Contact Resolution, Customer Sentiment and Temper Shift</strong> — see the glossary in section 12.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Insights</h3>\n<p>Every call, identified: residential or commercial; sales, service or warranty; product; and how it was handled. Click any row to hear those calls. Insights also holds <strong>Repeat Callers</strong> (numbers that called 3+ times in one day) and <strong>When calls come in</strong> (calls inside and outside each brand's hours).</p>\n<h3>Call trends</h3>\n<p>What callers are calling about: topics rising or falling this week versus the brand's normal, top reasons people call, objections, not-booked reasons, and booking rate by week.</p>\n<h3>Phone stats</h3>\n<p>Call center efficiency straight from LightSpeed, separate from QA. LightSpeed data arrives each morning for the day before.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Number</th>\n<th>What it means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Inbound CSR calls</td>\n<td>Every inbound call that reached a CSR queue or ring group, counted once</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Abandoned calls</td>\n<td>Callers who hung up waiting for a CSR. Rate = abandoned ÷ inbound CSR calls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Avg time to answer</td>\n<td>Seconds from reaching the CSR queue to pickup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Abandoned in the phone menu</td>\n<td>Hung up before any CSR queue rang — not in the abandon rate</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Below these: calls and abandons by hour or day, abandons by brand and location, and <strong>CSR Phone Activity</strong> for every front-line CSR. Switchboard may show slightly different numbers because some of its dashboards count a different set of queues.</p>\n<h3>Brands</h3>\n<p>One row per brand. Click a brand for its profile: an AI summary of why it's trending this way, Week by Week trend for the last 12 weeks, every CSR by location, recent calls, transfers and sentiment.</p>\n<h3>CSRs</h3>\n<p>One row per CSR with scored calls, average QA score, change, booking rate and card ask rate. Use the search box to find anyone. Click a CSR for their profile, including an AI summary of how to coach them.</p>",
