"id": "4-call-reviews",
"title": "4. Call reviews",
"html": "<p>Call reviews is where you find, hear and correct individual calls.</p>\n<h3>Finding a call</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open <strong>Call reviews</strong> from the left menu, or click any number elsewhere in the portal.</li>\n<li>Narrow the list with the filters: outcome (booked, not booked, transferred), call-flow step missed, score range, controllable misses, or quick lists such as <strong>Upset customers</strong>, <strong>Low scores (40 or under)</strong> and <strong>Booked, card not asked</strong>.</li>\n<li>Search by CSR, customer or phone number.</li>\n<li>Press ▶ to listen from the list, or click the row for the full review.</li>\n<li><strong>Copy link</strong> shares the exact filtered list with a teammate.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Reading a review</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Caller wanted</strong> — what the customer called about.</li>\n<li><strong>Score and outcome</strong> — the 0–100 QA score, booked or not booked, and whether a miss was in the CSR's control.</li>\n<li><strong>Detailed scoring</strong> — each call-flow step, the points earned, and the AI's reason. Press <strong>▶ Play this step</strong> to jump to that moment.</li>\n<li><strong>Biggest revenue lever</strong> and <strong>Coaching note</strong> — the one thing that would most likely have booked the call.</li>\n<li><strong>Transcript</strong> — click any line to play from there. Card details are removed.</li>\n<li><strong>Transfers</strong> — if the call was transferred, both legs are linked so you can follow the customer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Calls that weren't a sales or service opportunity (billing, status checks, asking for a person) show <strong>Not counted in QA scores</strong> and don't affect anyone's score.</p>\n<h3>Asking the AI about a call</h3>\n<p>Click <strong>Ask AI about this call</strong> and type a question, such as \"What did the customer say about price?\" The AI answers from the recording and transcript.</p>\n<h3>Changing a score you disagree with</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>On the step that's wrong, click <strong>Request change</strong> (admins see <strong>Change score</strong>).</li>\n<li>Pick the right answer and say what you heard, with a time if you can — for example \"She asked how can I help at 0:28.\"</li>\n<li>Only account admins can change a score, and it updates right away. Everyone else sends a request; the score changes only if an account admin approves it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The original AI score is always kept. Every change is logged with who made it and why. Corrections your team keeps making turn into <strong>Suggested scoring rules</strong> (section 9) so the AI learns.</p>\n<h3>Notes, kudos and printing</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Add note</strong> — leave a coaching note on the call for your team.</li>\n<li><strong>♥ Send kudos</strong> — send the CSR recognition for a great call.</li>\n<li><strong>Print / save PDF</strong> — a clean copy of the review.</li>\n</ul>",
